1... { -KEY- } Kc4 $1 { Obstruction. } ( { The more straightforward } 1... Kb3 $2 { only draws after } 2. Kd5 Kxb2 3. Ke6 Kc3 4. Kxe7 Kd4 5. Kf6 Ke4 6. Kg5 $1 { etc. } ) 
2. b4 { Obviously, the king couldn't move due to 2...e5, and } ( 2. b3 { leads to the same thing after } Kxb3 3. Kd5 Kc3 ) 
Kxb4 3. Kd5 Kc3 4. Ke6 Kd4 $1 { The king should stay close to its counterpart in order to obstruct it on the next move. } ( { In contrast, } 4... Kd3 $2 5. Kxe7 Ke3 6. Kf6 Kf3 7. Kg5 { is a draw. } ) 
5. Kxe7 Ke5 $1 6. Kf7 Kf5 { A last twist of obstruction. } ( { The move order matters: after } 6... h4 $2 7. gxh4 Kf5 8. h5 $1 h6 9. Ke7 Kg5 10. Ke6 Kxh5 11. Kf5 { the white king arrives on time. } ) 
7. Kg7 h4 $1 ( { Seeing that } 7... Kg4 8. Kh6 $1 { draws, Black swaps the pawns in a different way. } ) 
8. gxh4 h5 $1 9. Kf7 ( { Or } 9. Kh6 Kg4 10. Kg6 Kxh4 11. Kf5 Kg3 { with similar play. } ) 
Kg4 10. Kf6 Kxh4 11. Kf5 Kg3 12. Ke4 h4 13. Ke3 Kg2 
